id: pm-http-95t1
title: Recover concurrent journaled sends
description: ""
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-28T23:30:37.952Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-29T09:14:02.050Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: SDK expected-revision mutations; competing write and crash at every send boundary; stable operation identity converges without duplicate requests or observations.
parent: pm-http-76jn
comments[9]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-28T23:41:23.284Z",codex-agent,"Implemented journaled sends with eight deterministic protocol boundaries, stable operation identities and revision-guarded SDK state. Every interrupted possible send converges to stored evidence or explicit uncertainty without replay; two concurrent identities preserve both observations."
  "2026-10-29T00:26:01.227Z",codex-agent,"Independent-process acceptance passed 9/9: distinct writers and shared operation identity, plus SIGKILL at all eight send/record boundaries. Native dead leases recover and stable reruns admit exactly one observation, with at most one request. Logical interleaving and interruption schedules also pass 16/16."
  "2026-10-29T05:42:43.430Z",codex-agent,"PR 1 re-review: close the effect-admission class. Carry caller revision in durable plans, re-read the native item/probe immediately before any send, and refuse stale context. Public SDK limitations #1576 and #1620 leave a documented re-read-to-send window. Reserve sufficient state capacity before effects; concurrent writes must preserve in-flight recording capacity. Search all CLI, SDK, recovery and packed consumer paths; add adversarial no-git fixtures and behavioral revert proofs."
  "2026-10-29T06:11:25.499Z",codex-agent,"Focused results: admission corpus passed 6/6, plus the post-commit native-writer race passed 1/1; existing mutation/redaction/contention checks passed 3/3. Guarded planned recovery succeeds unchanged, refuses stale native comments, and retains the original caller revision. Legacy unreserved plans upgrade capacity before effects. Typecheck, ESLint, zero-duplication and docstring checks passed. Final source verification and behavioral revert proofs continue."
  "2026-10-29T06:36:10.576Z",codex-agent,"Review proof complete: six admission/media/shape/legacy behavioral reverts plus two exact-byte/transition-budget reverts passed (8 distinct scenarios). Each removed protection failed by assertion in a disposable copy; restored behavior passed. Capacity and legacy admission were rechecked after UTF-8 and revision-headroom refinements (2/2). Tracker-linked tests passed 7/7 at 2469be5; the latest boundary subset passed 3/3, exact byte-boundary property passed 1/1, and late SDK lease recovery passed 1/1. Packed npm/npx and Bun/bunx consumers passed 2/2 with guarded SDK calls and CLI capacity refusals in both formats. Final unchanged-threshold release checks follow the final evidence commit."
  "2026-10-29T07:19:48.346Z",codex-agent,"Additional class audit: effect-guard enforcement must be bound to the caller/initial plan, not selected by mutable journal fields. Adding adversarial journal-field erasure and recovered revision-rebase cases before final push. The prior final-head gates are retained as evidence for 560e3de; any resulting source change receives fresh npm and Bun gates."
  "2026-10-29T07:55:54.473Z",codex-agent,"Confirmed additional revision-class defects with three failing adversarial tests against 560e3de: mutable guard erasure, unguarded lifecycle/ownership changes, and recovered counter rebasing could permit effects. Fixed by binding unconditional checkpoint validation to the invocation's original caller policy and phase offsets. Cancellation now preserves completed or reassigned journal evidence. All three adversarial tests passed after the fix, and planned preview/completed/refused identity checks passed separately. The new checkpoint-removal proof and exact historical send-function revert both fail by assertion, then pass restored; revised admission and pre-send revert cases passed 4/4 together."
  "2026-10-29T09:08:15.245Z",codex-agent,"Closed the admission-policy class across fresh sends, planned recovery, previews, persisted declarations, and packed non-git consumers. Immutable caller guard and operation identity are rechecked at both effect checkpoints; erasing or rebasing a guard cannot opt out. Pending reservations must be valid and remain owned until recording. Declaration capacity is checked before schema registration. Three additional function-only mutations (reservation integrity, stored declaration validation, and schema preflight) each fail their adversarial test with the protection removed and pass after restoration: 3/3. Together with eight earlier review scenarios and two immutable-policy scenarios, thirteen new review revert scenarios are proven; fourteen original scenarios remain retained. No test or gate threshold was weakened. The documented SDK re-read-to-send window remains subject to upstream issues 1576 and 1620."
  "2026-10-29T09:13:56.235Z",codex-agent,"Final-source tracker-linked adversarial suite passed 7/7 with no skipped tests in an isolated snapshot. Packed npm/npx and bun/bunx non-git investigations passed 2/2, including SDK guard/lifecycle refusal and both CLI renderers. Typecheck, ESLint, zero duplication and all 93 documented declarations passed. Source is frozen for fresh npm and Bun release gates after this evidence commit. Remaining SDK windows are documented and tracked by pm-http-a8z1."
